### Deletion of the Head of a Linked List

**Problem:** Given the head of a singly linked list, delete the first node (head) of the linked list and return the head of the modified linked list.

**Approach:**

- Check if the linked list is empty (`head == null`). If so, return `null`.
- Store the next node of the head in a temporary reference.
- Update the head to point to the next node (`head = head.next`).
- The previous head is no longer part of the linked list.
- Return the updated head.
- If the linked list contains only one node, the updated head becomes `null`.

**Time Complexity:** O(1) – Only the head reference is updated.

**Space Complexity:** O(1) – No extra data structures are used.

**Concepts Used:**
- Singly Linked List
- Head Pointer
- Node Deletion
- Reference Manipulation
- Null Checking

###Solution

class Solution {
    public ListNode deleteHead(ListNode head) {
        //your code goes here
        if(head==null || head.next==null) return null;
        head=head.next;
        return head;
    }
}
